{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the sparse-set or the archetype storage for a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus"},{"type":"text","text":", and know what changes."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage"},"kind":"article","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"title":"Choosing a storage","roleHeading":"Article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps its entities and components in one of two storages, chosen when it is created:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let nexus = Nexus()                       \/\/ the default, same as Nexus(storage: .archetype)","let churning = Nexus(storage: .sparseSet) \/\/ for heavy add\/remove churn"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both storages offer the same API with the same observable behavior: generational entity identifiers, events, the structural lock and its traps, families, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"type":"text","text":", spans, snapshots, cloning and the entity state machine. Every test of the package runs against both. What differs is where the components live in memory, and with it what is cheap."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", so ","type":"text"},{"code":"Nexus()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" uses it. Choose ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" explicitly for workloads dominated by heavy component add and remove churn (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). There is no storage protocol: the set of storages is closed, and a nexus switches on its storage once per call, so each storage compiles to concrete code.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"The sparse-set storage","anchor":"The-sparse-set-storage","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps one dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type that maps an entity to its slot in that array, and a bitset of component types per entity. Adding or removing a component touches the data of that one type only, and no other component moves. Looking up one component is a sparse index read plus an array read."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family is the weak spot: the members of a family are stored in each component array in the order the components were added, so every extra component type costs a lookup per member, and the reads are scattered once the arrays were shuffled by churn."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"The-archetype-storage","text":"The archetype storage"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" follows the design of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": entities with exactly the same component types live in one table, with a column (an array) per component type. An index maps every entity to its table and row. Tables are created when a component set appears first, and adding or removing one component type moves the entity’s row to another table along a cached edge of the table graph.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family visits the tables that match it, and walks their columns linearly: no lookup per member and a sequential read per component. The list of matching tables is cached per family, which the nexus lists when the family is created and extends when a new table appears. A table that became empty stays alive, along with its columns and its entry in the cached lists, where an iteration skips it. Cleaning the nexus with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()"},{"type":"text","text":" drops all tables."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In flecs this is the default, and sparse components are the opt-in trait (","type":"text"},{"code":"Sparse","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"): “Sparse components are stored outside of tables, which means they do not have to be moved”, trading query speed for component add and remove speed (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). Fireblade 1.x was the reverse, a sparse set per component type; the two storages make that a choice per nexus instead of per component.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"What-the-numbers-say","text":"What the numbers say"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Measured with 10 000 entities, release build, Apple silicon, wall clock p50 per pass (","type":"text"},{"code":"make benchmark","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", see ","type":"text"},{"code":"Benchmarks\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Case","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sparse set","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Archetype","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"11 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2.5 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"18 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"4.3 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, B, C, D)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"31 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"7.7 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, writing: B)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"17 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"4.4 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B, writing: C)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"23 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"6.1 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 10% of the entities match"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"3.6 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1.3 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 100 000 entities with shuffled storage order","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"227 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"27 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 1 024 different component sets","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"18 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"11 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Parameter pack, 5 reads and 2 writes","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 200 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1 800 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"code":"for","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" over a family, 2 components"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Random ","type":"text"},{"code":"entity.get","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of one component, 10 000 lookups","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"334 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"345 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a component to each entity and remove it again, 10 000 entities","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 180 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4 900 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Create and destroy 1 000 entities with 7 components","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"1 730 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2 510 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"alignments":["left","right","right"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Fireblade 1.x needed 480 μs for the plain iteration of one component and 1 220 μs for two ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IterOnlyOneComponent"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IterOnlyTwoComponents"},{"type":"text","text":"). Both storages iterate without any allocation."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating with "},{"code":"forEach(reading:writing:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is 1.6 to 8 times faster on the archetype storage: about 4 times in the plain case, 8 times when the sparse-set arrays are shuffled against each other, and least when the entities are spread over many small tables."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Changing the component set of an entity costs about twice as much on the archetype storage: the whole row moves. An entity that changes its component set less than once in a few frames is far ahead on iteration; a world that toggles a component on most entities every frame is better off with the sparse set.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"for","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" iteration and random access cost the same on both: they look every component up per entity.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Entity creation and destruction are a bit slower on the archetype storage, because the row of every component moves with the entity."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Which-storage-to-pick","level":3,"text":"Which storage to pick"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default is the archetype storage: it iterates faster (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and iteration is what most worlds spend their time on."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off: the archetype storage buys iteration speed with the cost of moving a row whenever the component set of an entity changes. Prefer "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet"},{"type":"text","text":" when the workload is dominated by heavy add and remove churn, for example toggling a component on most entities every frame. This matches flecs, where sparse components are the opt-in trait for components that are added and removed often."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Differences-you-can-observe","level":3,"text":"Differences you can observe"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration order."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The sparse-set storage visits the members of a family in the order of the family’s member list, the archetype storage table by table and row by row, and rows move when entities change tables. Neither order is a contract; use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or your own key if you need one."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Single-type spans."}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)"},{"text":" view one contiguous array. On the archetype storage a type is stored in one column per table, so if entities with different component sets have the type, the span views a temporary copy made table by table (and the writing variant stores it back when the closure returns, also when it throws). That costs one allocation and a copy per call, and nothing can observe the difference while the closure runs, because the type is locked.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Family spans.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)"},{"text":" passes one batch per matching table on the archetype storage, however the nexus was used before; the sparse-set storage passes shorter batches after churn. Both visit every member exactly once, and the closure must be correct for any batch size.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents"},{"text":" for the spans.","type":"text"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Benchmarks":{"role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"See how FirebladeECS revisions compare on a shared workload suite, and run the comparison yourself."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/benchmarks","title":"Benchmarks","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEvent":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A marker protocol for all Nexus events."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NexusEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexusevent","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NexusEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"NexusEvent","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/sparseSet":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type, a bitset per entity."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/sparseset","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sparseSet","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Nexus.StorageKind.sparseSet","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/clear()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Clears all data from the Nexus."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()","type":"topic","title":"clear()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"clear"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/clear()","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say","title":"What the numbers say","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage#What-the-numbers-say","kind":"section","abstract":[],"type":"topic"},"https://www.flecs.dev/flecs/md_docs_2Queries.html":{"title":"flecs","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"flecs","type":"text"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","url":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/MigratingToFirebladeECS2":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Move a project from FirebladeECS 1.x to 2.0: components become value types, and every write goes through the nexus.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/migratingtofirebladeecs2","title":"Migrating to FirebladeECS 2","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReactingToNexusEvents":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Observe structural changes and, on request, changes of component values."}],"title":"Reacting to Nexus events","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/reactingtonexusevents","role":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(reading:_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Gives ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":" read access to all components of a type as one contiguous ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Span"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"componentSpan(reading:_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"componentSpan","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"reading","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".Type, (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Span","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SpanV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rethrows","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/componentspan(reading:_:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS":{"type":"topic","title":"Getting started with Fireblade ECS","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/gettingstartedwithfirebladeecs","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn the API and key types Fireblade provides to compose your game or app logic."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","kind":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventMask":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The kinds of events a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" subscribes to."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NexusEventMask","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexuseventmask","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NexusEventMask","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"NexusEventMask","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReadingAndWritingComponents":{"kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read a copy, replace a component or change it in place."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/readingandwritingcomponents","title":"Reading and writing components","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Family/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)":{"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"each C","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Component"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"title":"forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Iterates the members of this family in batches, giving ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the components of a batch as contiguous spans."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"forEachComponentSpan"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"R1"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W1"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"text":"reading","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"R1"},{"text":".Type, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"writing","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W1","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".Type, (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Span","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIden